          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Connecting a tech stack that spans **ERP, CRM, MYOB Acumatica (formerly MYOB Advanced), SAP, and Microsoft 365** requires an integration specialist with cross-platform expertise, rather than a single-vendor reseller. \n\nSeveral system integration specialists and mid-market ERP consultancies in Melbourne are equipped to connect these specific platforms:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Dual-Ecosystem Specialists (MYOB Acumatica + SAP + Microsoft)\n\n#### **Cloud Factory** *(Melbourne CBD)*\n* **Best for:** Mid-market businesses running or bridging between MYOB Acumatica and SAP.\n* **Why them:** Uniquely, Cloud Factory holds certified partnerships across **MYOB Acumatica**, **SAP Business One**, and **Microsoft Dynamics 365/Power Platform**. Because their engineering team actively deploys and configures both MYOB and SAP ecosystems, they understand data schema differences (e.g., GL structures, inventory valuations, order workflows) when building bridges between them, CRMs, and Microsoft 365.\n\n#### **Leverage Technologies** *(Melbourne)*\n* **Best for:** Integrated CRM and multi-ERP architecture.\n* **Why them:** Like Cloud Factory, Leverage Technologies is one of the few Australian consultancies with established practices in both **SAP** (SAP Business One) and **MYOB Acumatica**. They specialize heavily in CRM-to-ERP synchronisation and have deep experience connecting back-office operations to modern Microsoft cloud stacks.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Dedicated Middleware & API Integrators\n\n#### **MyIntegrator** *(South Melbourne)*\n* **Best for:** Turnkey, real-time sync pipelines and iPaaS-driven integration.\n* **Why them:** MyIntegrator is a dedicated system integration house headquartered in South Melbourne. Rather than just acting as an ERP vendor, they specialise in building continuous data feeds and custom APIs between disparate platforms. They possess pre-built connectors and custom middleware logic explicitly for MYOB Acumatica, SAP, various CRMs (Salesforce, HubSpot, Zoho), and external databases.\n\n#### **Communicat IT** *(Melbourne)*\n* **Best for:** API-first integration and Microsoft 365 / Power Platform automation.\n* **Why them:** Communicat IT focuses heavily on modern, API-first integrations connecting ERP systems (including SAP and MYOB) directly into the **Microsoft 365 / Power Platform** ecosystem. If your goal is to pull live ERP/CRM data into SharePoint, Teams, Power Apps, or automated approvals via Microsoft 365, their delivery model is tailored directly to this.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Enterprise-Scale Systems Integrator\n\n#### **Atturra** *(Melbourne Hub)*\n* **Best for:** Larger or complex enterprise environments (e.g., SAP S/4HANA, Salesforce, multi-subsidiary workflows).\n* **Why them:** Atturra is one of Australia’s leading listed system integrators and an elite integration/Boomi/Microsoft partner. If your SAP footprint is enterprise-tier (S/4HANA rather than Business One) or your data governance requirements are strict, Atturra’s Data & Integration arm excels at enterprise middleware architecture (Azure Integration Services, Boomi, MuleSoft) to orchestrate CRM, ERP, and Microsoft 365 flows.\n\n---\n\n### 4. MYOB Acumatica Native Specialist\n\n#### **Kilimanjaro Consulting** *(Melbourne Office)*\n* **Best for:** Ensuring MYOB Acumatica remains the clean, primary source of truth.\n* **Why them:** Kilimanjaro is the largest and most recognised MYOB Enterprise / Acumatica Diamond Partner in Australia. While their core business is MYOB deployment, they have in-house integration developers who build custom bridges between Acumatica, external CRMs, third-party logistics/SAP feeds, and Microsoft 365 reporting environments.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Selection Guide\n\n| If your primary challenge is... | Consider contacting... |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Connecting mid-market MYOB Acumatica + SAP Business One + CRM** | **Cloud Factory** or **Leverage Technologies** |\n| **Custom APIs, continuous data sync, or automated data ingestion** | **MyIntegrator** |\n| **Deep Microsoft 365, Power Automate, and SharePoint integration with ERPs** | **Communicat IT** |\n| **Complex, enterprise-scale data orchestration (e.g., SAP S/4HANA / Enterprise CRM)** | **Atturra** |\n\n### Key Question to Ask Providers Before Engaging\n* **Middleware strategy:** Ask whether they build **custom point-to-point webhooks** or utilize an **iPaaS / Azure Logic Apps / Boomi** layer. For an ecosystem touching ERP, CRM, and Microsoft 365, an iPaaS or Azure Integration Services approach will ensure failure alerting, transactional retries, and lower maintenance costs as APIs change.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
          "role": "model"
        },
